WEBVTT

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.290
"Smile Down the Runway"

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:40.620
"Operation in progress"

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:53.870
"Episode 8: The Designer's Capacity"
No... Please... Mother...

00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:59.790
It's okay.

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:01.290
It's going to be okay.

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:08.200
You're unbelievable! What took you so long?!

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:10.790
This is terrible...

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:13.080
I found this on her wrinkled bed.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:14.540
I was alone when I found it.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:17.370
"Dear Ikuto, Honoka, Aoi and Ichika"
I was alone when I found it.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.700
What was I supposed to do?!

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:26.160
Honoka.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:32.700
She kept it from us in order to protect us.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.250
I can't bear this! I can't believe
she would do such thing!

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:46.950
Are you okay?

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:48.120
Yup.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:50.910
Did you talk to Ichika and Aoi?

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:52.540
Not yet.

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:55.910
Then, could you tell Aoi secretly?

00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:58.250
Don't let Ichika find out.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:08.000
I'm sure they're worried sick. Could you
let them know everything's all right?

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.330
Okay.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:24.790
She wasn't doing well at all...

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:27.790
Mommy, what are you doing?

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:33.040
I'm using your old clothes
to make Honoka's skirt.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.580
I want to do it, too!

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:38.500
Not yet. It's still too dangerous for you.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:41.620
She was repeatedly hospitalized...

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.870
You've already surpassed Mommy
with your skills, Ikuto.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:48.370
Wh-What?

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:51.700
Honoka won't even bother with me.

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:55.580
Why did I believe her
when she said she was okay?

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:06.410
Don't worry. Mommy's with you.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:09.580
Mommy's here for all of you.

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:18.450
I'm trying not to dwell on the past.

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:22.120
But I kept getting hospitalized.

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:28.160
I thought it would only be one time.
But I kept relapsing...

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:31.750
I started losing hope.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:38.540
I'm so sorry. The savings
your father left for you...

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:41.540
I ended up using it all.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:45.790
But that's not going to stop me
from being positive.

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:48.250
Sure, I didn't have the luck or the energy...

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:56.120
But Honoka got into her dream school, Aoi has
her volleyball, and Ichika loves pre-school...

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:59.410
It's truly amazing.

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:02.250
But let me tell you, Ikuto.

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:08.040
I don't even want to think about
if you hadn't been there.

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:14.830
Mother... I want to be a fashion designer.

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:18.000
Ah...

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:24.080
I know... I know, Ikuto.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:29.500
Ikuto... Thank you for all
that you have endured.

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:32.410
I'm sorry.

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:36.080
If there is still more for you to endure...

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:42.160
No matter how positive I've been,
I would regret that.

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:48.330
I have every intention to recover...
But... Just in case...

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:54.500
If something happens to me,
there will be some money for you.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:57.330
Use half of the money for yourself, Ikuto.

00:05:57.330 --> 00:06:00.450
Use it for yourself, okay?

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:04.660
Why... Why would you think
you'd disappear like this?

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:23.250
"Paris/Moscow"

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:27.410
No response from Ikuto, after all...

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:31.790
He must be really busy.

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:37.250
I better do my best, too.

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:39.450
"Hayasaka General Hospital"

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:45.160
The operation was successful. Her post-operative
progress is satisfactory as well.

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:48.160
However...

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:53.950
She is susceptible to relapse
if she pushes herself too much.

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:58.080
We advised her to have
the operation much earlier.

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:02.540
But she was adamant about
waiting another two months.

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:04.700
Two months...?

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:07.120
So when is that Geika Festival happening?

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:09.450
In two months!

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:11.040
How exciting.

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:15.790
It was my fault...

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:22.620
If her recovery goes well,
she can be released in a month.

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:24.700
Thank you very much.

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:32.750
And... We've been consulting with your mother
for a few months regarding the bill.

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:34.410
Oh.

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:39.580
The entire balance for her treatment
is due upon her release.

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:48.330
I see... Mother... You had
nothing left in your savings...

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:52.370
460,000 yen by next month...?

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:54.580
I'm way behind.

00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:59.290
Oh?

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:02.080
"Inbox"
"Miss Chiyuki"

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:03.290
"I'm off to Paris!"

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:09.200
It's okay.

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:11.200
I'll take care of it.

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:16.540
Oh...

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:22.750
Then, here's your next task.

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:25.080
Oh! Right away!

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:28.620
Ah, it must be him.

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:33.660
Mr. Ayano. I'm sorry for barging in like this.

00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:35.120
Um...

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:43.080
Oh. Sorry, you two.
Could you give us a minute?

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:45.790
We need to stop everything for him?

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:48.250
Please, Kanami.

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:50.000
O-Oh...

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:54.620
I'm sorry...

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:00.200
So? What's going on?

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:04.040
O-Oh... Um... Well, I...

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:09.000
If you don't have anything to say, could you
go back to helping Yusuke and them like usual?

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:11.580
Things are really busy at the moment.

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:15.580
Please let me quit.

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:17.370
Why?

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:19.660
Oh... Well...

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:20.700
Ikuto.

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:27.250
I don't know why you're hesitant to tell me.
But I'm your employer.

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:30.580
I have the right to ask, at least.

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:35.950
Actually...

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:41.250
I see. Your mother...

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:47.540
You want to quit to take up multiple
part-time jobs because you need the money.

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:48.830
Yes.

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:53.870
Well if that's the case,
I didn't need to be so worried.

00:09:53.870 --> 00:09:56.870
I can definitely help you out with that.

00:09:56.870 --> 00:09:58.200
Ikuto.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:01.290
Welcome to my team.

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:02.540
What...?

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:05.660
Not as a part-timer, but as an official
team member who works for my brand

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:09.330
which will be number one at the Geika Festival.

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:11.830
What? Hold on a minute.

00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:14.700
Mr. Ayano, were you even listening to me?

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:16.910
Yeah, I heard you.

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:22.830
You're thinking, "How could I work here
when I decided to quit Hajime's," right?

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:24.250
But why?

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:28.200
It's not worth worrying about
that kind of thing.

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:35.160
I'm only seeing your potential
as a patternmaker.

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:38.080
With you on board, Ikuto,
this year's Geika Festival--

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:40.370
Please, I really don't understand.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:45.000
I'm entering the finals myself.
If I join your team, Mr. Ayano...

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:47.540
Huh? What are you saying?

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.290
What?

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:52.830
You're going to fill up your days
working at part-time jobs, right?

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:57.250
Consider your time... the materials...
When will you have time to make anything?

00:10:57.250 --> 00:10:59.580
You have to be realistic.

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:01.200
Um...

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:04.410
Don't think you know better
than someone who

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:10.500
devotes their mind and body
24 hours a day to their craft.

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:14.160
I can't just give up like this.

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:17.040
"Use it for yourself."
I can't just give up like this.

00:11:17.790 --> 00:11:23.580
I'll sacrifice sleep and take apart old clothes
to prepare something for the finals.

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:25.040
Ikuto.

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:28.080
For you to think you have that kind of talent?

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:30.120
It's laughable.

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:35.160
Since we're on this, let me
set you straight with the truth.

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:37.910
Ikuto, your talent as a designer

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:41.450
is average or even below average.

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:46.080
You don't have the capacity
to make a living as a designer.

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:50.750
Take this chance to give up
and aim to be a patternmaker.

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:53.750
Or...

00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:56.330
"Post-Graduation Plans
Ikuto Tsumura
First Choice: Find employment."
Continue living in extreme poverty

00:11:56.330 --> 00:12:00.870
by sacrificing even more
things to cling onto the designer path.

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:05.330
Is that the life you desire?

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:08.200
Ikuto, I mean well.

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:10.540
Just join my team.

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:16.080
Then, I'll cover your mother's medical expenses.

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:18.450
I promise.

00:12:18.450 --> 00:12:20.000
Okay?

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:30.450
What does he know? What does he know?
What does he know?

00:12:30.450 --> 00:12:33.540
I'm so frustrated!

00:12:33.540 --> 00:12:37.910
For me, it doesn't matter
if I have the talent or not...

00:12:37.910 --> 00:12:40.540
I just want to do the things I enjoy!

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:50.620
I don't have money...

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:55.750
What do you expect
from a high schooler?!

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:59.540
I didn't choose to be born poor.

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:03.370
I wasn't born with a silver spoon
in my mouth like you, Mr. Ayano!

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:05.830
You have no right to tell me anything!

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:12.750
Just as I thought. I knew I'd run into you
if I waited around the school.

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:14.750
Huh?

00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:16.330
You're...

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:19.200
What do you want?

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:22.250
I know you're struggling with money.

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:24.040
Let's make a deal.

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:27.450
<i>Smile Down the Runway.</i>

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:29.870
"Geika Fashion School"

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:32.700
I don't understand what you're saying.

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:35.040
You know exactly what I'm saying.

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:39.080
I conducted an investigation since
Hasegawa's been acting strange lately.

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:41.290
And it all leads to you.

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:44.160
What...? An investigation...?

00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:47.500
From your mother's condition
to your family situation...

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:51.540
I even know how much influence
you have on Hasegawa.

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:54.540
You need the money, right?

00:13:54.540 --> 00:14:00.450
In exchange for this money, convince Hasegawa
to give up on becoming a designer.

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:01.620
Ugh!

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:07.370
Why...?

00:14:07.370 --> 00:14:10.330
Why does everyone...

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:15.870
...try to take advantage of what's
most valuable to me in such selfish ways?

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:20.950
Don't sweat it. You need it, right?

00:14:20.950 --> 00:14:25.160
I'm in a position where I'm responsible
for Hasegawa's future.

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:29.750
I don't irresponsibly encourage her
to gamble with her life like you do.

00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:31.620
Irresponsibly...?!

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:34.580
You're only saying that because you don't know
how hard Miss Kokoro's working!

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:36.330
If hard work...

00:14:36.330 --> 00:14:41.950
If this is a world where hard work pays off...
Why isn't the tiny model a star yet?

00:14:43.620 --> 00:14:47.330
Hasegawa will listen to you.

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:51.290
I'm coming to you with complete faith.

00:14:51.290 --> 00:14:53.540
With this money...

00:14:53.540 --> 00:15:00.790
...you can cover your mother's medical expenses
and still have enough for the festival.

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:04.700
And this isn't a bad thing for Hasegawa, either.

00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:05.540
I can't do that!

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:07.750
Ikuto Tsumura.

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:11.830
Just tell her this and everyone's happy.

00:15:11.830 --> 00:15:16.000
"Will you appear in my show as a model?"

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:26.040
Contact me anytime.

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:27.250
"Bon Rouge Manager Yu Igarashi"

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:31.790
I'm looking forward to seeing you
and Hasegawa's show.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:45.540
Mr. Ikuto's quilting...?

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:46.790
Ugh...

00:15:46.790 --> 00:15:48.580
I-I'm so sorry!

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:50.160
Bob's quitting.

00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:52.450
H-He's quitting?

00:15:52.450 --> 00:15:54.080
What is he quitting?

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:55.660
Here.

00:15:55.660 --> 00:15:58.370
Here...? You must be kidding...

00:15:59.950 --> 00:16:03.290
You are... aren't you?

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:04.160
But why?

00:16:04.160 --> 00:16:05.910
Not my business.

00:16:05.910 --> 00:16:09.620
Oh, no... I need to call him...

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:13.370
But how could I be of help?

00:16:13.370 --> 00:16:16.370
He's the one who always helps me...

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:19.750
For someone as strong as him to quit...

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:22.790
...it must be something serious.

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:24.290
But...

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:27.120
May I please call him right now?

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:34.950
I don't care if you do, but you're
on the clock. Keep quiet.

00:16:34.950 --> 00:16:36.500
Ah...

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:39.160
Mr. Ikuto...

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:47.870
And... will you give me Mr. Ayano's number?

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:49.450
He might know something.

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:51.250
Hey, Big One. Are you deaf?

00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:53.080
I'll keep quiet!

00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:55.500
I'll keep quiet, so...

00:16:55.500 --> 00:16:58.750
Please don't let him quit!

00:16:58.750 --> 00:17:00.410
There must be...

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:03.580
There must be a reason for it...!

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:04.910
Please!

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:06.250
Oh...

00:17:11.910 --> 00:17:15.370
Mr. Ikuto... Where are you...?

00:17:15.370 --> 00:17:16.950
Mr. Ikuto...

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:23.120
I was only given two months.

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:26.830
I took up as many jobs as possible.

00:17:26.830 --> 00:17:28.950
Even Honoka got a job.

00:17:28.950 --> 00:17:32.410
Aoi's helping out with the chores.

00:17:32.410 --> 00:17:38.000
We're all working hard for our living
expenses and little savings.

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:41.370
Only three weeks until the Geika Festival...

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:46.950
I can't think of a design...

00:17:46.950 --> 00:17:50.700
For you to think you have that
kind of talent? It's laughable.

00:17:51.830 --> 00:17:54.330
Ikuto, the bath's all yours.

00:17:54.330 --> 00:17:55.580
Okay.

00:17:55.580 --> 00:17:56.790
Oh...

00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:04.200
Cheer up a bit, will you? You're already under
so much pressure. Don't make it any worse.

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:05.870
Take a bath to refresh yourself.

00:18:05.870 --> 00:18:07.950
Leave me alone!

00:18:07.950 --> 00:18:12.000
I'm exhausted. I need my quiet.

00:18:16.250 --> 00:18:18.750
Sorry to bother you.

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:26.950
Ikuto, go take a bath.

00:18:26.950 --> 00:18:29.000
I'm the worst...!

00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:34.580
I'm sorry.

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:45.200
They wouldn't even let me walk two steps...

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:51.500
"Inbox"
"Miss Kokoro"

00:18:52.370 --> 00:18:58.790
No... I can't get Miss Kokoro involved
in this. I can't respond to her now.

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:07.040
Hey... I should be happy
earning money making clothes.

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:10.290
There's nothing wrong with
becoming a patternmaker.

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:16.040
All right. I should go apologize
to Mr. Ayano and thank him.

00:19:18.040 --> 00:19:19.290
Huh?

00:19:23.830 --> 00:19:26.500
Hello, do you have an appointment?

00:19:26.500 --> 00:19:30.750
U-Um... I was called in by President Fujito.

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:34.580
Sorry for calling you in so abruptly.

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:38.290
P-Please... It's been a while...

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:42.830
Don't be so rigid. Just relax.
Here, have a seat.

00:19:42.830 --> 00:19:47.080
May I ask... why you called me in today?

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:51.250
Actually, Chiyuki's returning from Paris today.

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:53.370
Huh? Oh...

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:55.160
Oh...

00:19:55.160 --> 00:20:01.000
Not one place gave her a chance,
and she ran out of funds.

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:04.410
Chiyuki talks about you a lot, Tsumura.

00:20:04.410 --> 00:20:07.790
You'll be able to cheer her up.

00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:11.700
I'd be grateful if you could talk to her.

00:20:11.700 --> 00:20:13.660
Ah...

00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:16.790
I'm not sure if I'm in
the right mindset for that...

00:20:16.790 --> 00:20:20.250
Ah... Why don't we relocate?

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:29.830
President Fujito. There's something
I need to apologize to you about.

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:32.700
Is it about you quitting Yanagida's?

00:20:32.700 --> 00:20:35.370
Ah... I'm sorry...

00:20:35.370 --> 00:20:38.120
It was you who introduced me to him...

00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:42.040
Well, there was always
a high turnover at Yanagida's.

00:20:42.040 --> 00:20:43.250
Ah.

00:20:43.250 --> 00:20:45.040
It's not like that.

00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:48.620
Mr. Yanagida didn't do anything wrong.

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:50.870
It's because I...

00:20:50.870 --> 00:20:54.080
I don't have anything...

00:20:58.410 --> 00:21:02.830
I have to apologize to you, too, Tsumura.

00:21:06.080 --> 00:21:08.950
I had you wait for so long.

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:10.700
Huh...?

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:12.950
What? That's...

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:20.410
Tsumura. I don't know all the details,
but I heard you were struggling financially.

00:21:20.410 --> 00:21:23.290
According to Yanagida.

00:21:23.290 --> 00:21:25.830
But how did Mr. Yanagida know...?

00:21:25.830 --> 00:21:27.750
I have a message for you from him.

00:21:27.750 --> 00:21:28.540
--Hello Mr. Ayano. I'm sorry to bother you,
but I'm calling about Mr. Ikuto.

00:21:28.540 --> 00:21:31.200
--"Thank Hasegawa."
--Hello Mr. Ayano. I'm sorry to bother you,
but I'm calling about Mr. Ikuto.

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:34.000
--Hello Mr. Ayano. I'm sorry to bother you,
but I'm calling about Mr. Ikuto.

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:35.660
Why...?

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:37.700
Tsumura...

00:21:37.700 --> 00:21:42.540
Do you remember when we first met?

00:21:42.540 --> 00:21:44.120
Yes...

00:21:44.120 --> 00:21:49.200
Will you let me fulfill that promise we made?

00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:50.660
What...?

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:59.000
I'd like to buy the design for
the outfit you made for Chiyuki.

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:01.910
I've got two million yen for you.

00:22:01.910 --> 00:22:05.660
That's too much... I can't accept it.

00:22:05.660 --> 00:22:09.580
Top designers get tens and hundreds
of millions for their designs.

00:22:09.580 --> 00:22:12.620
I'd say this is a fair assessment.

00:22:12.620 --> 00:22:16.750
President... Fujito...

00:22:16.750 --> 00:22:18.750
Do you think...

00:22:18.750 --> 00:22:23.080
...I could become... a fashion designer...?

00:22:24.660 --> 00:22:28.620
In my opinion, I'd be surprised if you didn't.

00:22:30.950 --> 00:22:38.200
Tsumura... Could I rely
on you to talk to Chiyuki?

00:22:43.200 --> 00:22:44.620
Miss Chiyuki!

00:22:46.450 --> 00:22:48.750
Um!

00:22:48.750 --> 00:22:51.580
Would you like to be in my show?

00:22:53.620 --> 00:22:57.660
Jeez... I guess if you're going to twist my arm.

00:24:31.830 --> 00:24:33.950
Next, "Rivals."

00:24:33.950 --> 00:24:36.910
"See you next time!!"
